Read the source data (CLDR's JSON, ICU's export data, Unicode's character data, the tzdb and
the segmenter's LSTM models) from local copies named by environment variables, instead of
downloading it (icu_provider_source without its networking feature); build without ICU4X's
compiled data (the data comes from those sources only); and find Chromium's tree from the
current directory, not from where the tool was built.

